<h1>Xiu Jin Qigong</h1>
<p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15em;color:#5A9EAD;" class="reveal">Seven exercises. Simple to learn, remarkably deep to practise.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:1.2em;" class="reveal"><a href="/why-qigong-training/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Why choose this training?</a></p>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>Xiu Jin Qigong is a compact set of seven exercises with an unusually wide effect on the meridian system. It is one of those rare practices that a beginner can pick up within weeks yet an experienced practitioner can keep refining for years - the depth is in the internal work, not in complicated choreography.</p>
</div>

<p class="reveal">That internal work is exactly what this course teaches. Copying the shapes of a Qigong exercise is easy; making those shapes do something is another matter entirely. The difference lies in stance, posture and focus - in the intention (Yi) guiding the Qi and in the felt, tangible feedback that tells you whether anything is actually happening. All of this is covered from the very first session, taught one to one by Seb.</p>

<h3 class="reveal">What Xiu Jin Works On</h3>
<p class="reveal">Within the traditional framework, the seven exercises of Xiu Jin:</p>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Stimulate the flow of Qi through the Yin and Yang meridians of the legs and arms, and across the twelve meridians as a whole</li>
<li>Give particular attention to the Kidney, Heart, Heart Governor (Pericardium) and Liver meridians</li>
<li>Open Ming Men, the "Gate of Life" on the lower back</li>
<li>Help clear Dazhui (Du 14), the point at the "big bone" where the neck meets the upper back</li>
<li>Help release Jianjing (GB 21) across the tops of the shoulders</li>
<li>Benefit the lower back and steadily strengthen the legs</li>
<li>Train the paired skills of sinking the Qi and raising the Shen - several of the exercises are an honest test of both</li>
<li>Improve posture, and through better posture give you cleaner access to your Qi</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="reveal">What You Will Learn</h3>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>All seven exercises, taught one at a time with room to absorb each</li>
<li>The stance, posture and focus each exercise requires</li>
<li>Which meridians and acupuncture points every movement addresses</li>
<li>How to sink the Qi while raising the Shen - and how to tell when you are genuinely doing it</li>
</ul>

